    {
      "id": "LCB-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "A bounded spherical coefficient bounds the eigenvalue of each finite Hecke sum",
      "anchor": "lifts-local-cartan-bound",
      "statement": "For a finite left K-stable set S of cosets gK, the Hecke indicator acts by a scalar a on the spherical eigenvector. A bounded coefficient c(g)=ℓ(ρ(g)x) with c(1)≠0 gives |a|≤#S.",
      "hypotheses": "Nonarchimedean local GLₙ(k) with K=GLₙ(𝒪), finite residue field of order q, and a spherical eigenvector carrying a Satake multiset. The scalar linear functional gives a bounded coefficient with nonzero value at the identity. Representatives may be chosen freely because x is K-fixed.",
