      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "Translate the eigenvector equation by every y and apply ℓ. Taking the supremum B=sup |c(y)| on the left gives |a|B≤#S·B, and 0<B<∞ permits division. The normalized spherical function with the same parameters therefore has finite-set sums of norm at most #S, regardless of its pointwise values.",
      "review": "Matched the supremum argument and the evaluation of the normalized model at the identity with the written proof. The supremum need not be attained. Independently checked the finiteness and positivity needed to cancel B."
    },
    {
      "id": "LCB-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Integral sublattices bound complete homogeneous polynomials in the scaled parameters",
      "anchor": "lifts-local-cartan-count",
